they last as long as possible so in this video&nbsp;
i'm going to talk about the expiration date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:17.280
on spices and herbs so with spices you usually&nbsp;
have different blends of dried roots bark or the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.880
stem and usually spices last anywhere between&nbsp;
two and three years then you have herbs which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:31.280
are the dried leaves like basil oregano thyme&nbsp;
rosemary mint bay leaves dill parsley cilantro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.520
sage and typically they will last anywhere between&nbsp;
one and three years but then we have the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:45.360
spices as in whole peppercorn coriander&nbsp;
mustard seeds fennel seeds caraway seeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:52.160
cumin seeds clove and cinnamon sticks which lasts&nbsp;
four years or even longer so you might want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.280
consider getting most of your herbs in a whole&nbsp;
form and then just get a grinder now what happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:03.280
when these herbs have an expired expiration date&nbsp;
well they're still okay to take they just might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.600
lose flavor potency and color but they're not&nbsp;
going to make you sick unless they have gotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.640
some moisture and there's some mold growing in&nbsp;
that product now i know in my pantry i probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:21.520
have herbs still in there from maybe seven even&nbsp;
10 years ago we still use them on occasion but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.600
they're just not as strong now when you're storing&nbsp;
herbs make sure they're in glass sealed bottles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.760
with the top really tight because air moisture and&nbsp;
light can degrade these herbs a lot faster make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.680
sure they're in a dark place and make sure they're&nbsp;
not exposed to heat so you wouldn't want to store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:44.480
